{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1411"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge society/business","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/society__business.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",774],["+","Heavy industry hides its history in its initials too. BASF, today the chemical group with the highest turnover in the world, was founded in Mannheim on 6 April 1865 as the Badische Anilin- & Soda-Fabrik. The A stands for Aniline, the coal-tar derivative from which the first synthetic dyes were made, and the S for soda; the works themselves were soon built on the other bank of the Rhine, in Ludwigshafen, where the company's headquarters still stand.\n\n"],["=",107],["+","\n| BASF | Badische Anilin- & Soda-Fabrik | 1865 |"],["=",96]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",692],["+","Auch die Schwerindustrie versteckt ihre Geschichte in Initialen. Die BASF, heute der umsatzstärkste Chemiekonzern der Welt, wurde am 6. April 1865 in Mannheim als Badische Anilin- & Soda-Fabrik gegründet. Das A steht für Anilin, das Teerderivat, aus dem die ersten synthetischen Farbstoffe hergestellt wurden, das S für Soda; das Werk selbst entstand bald am anderen Rheinufer in Ludwigshafen, wo der Konzern bis heute seinen Sitz hat.\n\n"],["=",107],["+","\n| BASF | Badische Anilin- & Soda-Fabrik | 1865 |"],["=",90]]}]},
